{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-proposition-algebraic-stack-no-automorphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-limits-proposition-characterize-locally-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:64aedc2458c70524650cc6eebb3cd8ac10b5525ba3987286dac7c2d7aca34f58", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:54cd894c63221006c00275769a534b91dbcc3ac47e63968e4ab193f875b6c055", "source_text": "Under each of the three assumptions <MATH_0001> is representable\nby an algebraic space <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003>, see Algebraic Stacks, Proposition\n<REF_0001>.\nIt is clear that (1) and (2) are equivalent as a functor between\nsetoids is an equivalence if and only if it is surjective on isomorphism\nclasses. Finally, (1) and (3) are equivalent by\nLimits of Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9a92263e19a0b2fd5ce0f56986e0c3035834995b644568a6e62b7f2bff9d7ada", "unit_id": "tag:07XN:proof"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:caa40be7ae69c2d026c53b1cf4e51a5e15e86264d0cb0c00865665221fdef712", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2c81c080f0b387ca0852a17d0175ecf2af825a702d1ace18068db3f45899f2f7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a category fibred\nin groupoids over <MATH_0003>. Assume\n<MATH_0004> is\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces and <MATH_0005> is limit preserving.\nThen <MATH_0006> is locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9e9f6699041d322d3cf8b62b420fc54442e466139fe4e7c8b370f45bdf849b4e", "unit_id": "tag:0CXI:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07XK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\theta$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$V$", "MATH_0007": "$F_\\theta$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_{\\Delta, \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}, \\theta}\n(\\Sch/V)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0009": "$f_\\theta : F_\\theta \\to V$", "MATH_0010": "$F_\\theta \\to V$", "MATH_0011": "$F_\\theta \\to S$", "MATH_0012": "$F_\\theta \\to V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{criteria-lemma-check-property-limit-preserving}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebraic-section-morphisms-representable-by-algebraic-spaces}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-product-limit-preserving}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-limit-preserving-algebraic-space}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-permanence-finite-type}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ab7b148c97cf8dc1c7867704a27fdd991f8b2af42d3811ebddebf614f6564ad8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e083723238fa19aac37fb59b88d41644d21ea4896d43b496f67f9cad97c22f7a", "source_text": "We apply Criteria for Representability, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme <MATH_0002> locally of finite presentation over <MATH_0003>\nand let <MATH_0004> be an object of <MATH_0005>\nover <MATH_0006>. Let <MATH_0007> be an algebraic space representing\n<MATH_0008> and let <MATH_0009> be the canonical morphism\n(see Algebraic Stacks, Section\n<REF_0002>).\nIt suffices to show that\n<MATH_0010> has the corresponding properties. By\nLemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004>\nwe see that <MATH_0011> is locally of finite presentation.\nIt follows that <MATH_0012> is locally of finite type\nby Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4c890486f2cc7771aab81423a1a92e5df57a52a3e64aba8635f2f2e74f58faaa", "unit_id": "tag:0CXI:proof"}
